description:
We are CDAI—the data and artificial intelligence engine of Compass Group North America. We design and deliver custom, in\-house solutions tailored to the unique complexities of food service and hospitality. Our work is grounded in strong data foundations, layered with AI to enhance forecasting, streamline operations, and enable better, faster decision\-making across Compass Group. With deep integration into the business and a commitment to white\-glove service, CDAI empowers associates, clients, and customers through innovative, future\-forward technologies.

**Job Summary**
---------------


Job Summary We are seeking a strategic and hands\-on AI Manager to lead our dynamic team of engineers and scientists in building innovative AI solutions. The ideal candidate combines technical expertise with strong leadership skills, excels in cross\-functional collaboration, and is passionate about translating advanced AI capabilities into real\-world impact. As an AI Manager, you will guide the development of advanced data products and AI\-powered applications, while shaping the roadmap, processes, and talent that drive long\-term success. You will partner closely with stakeholders across Engineering, Data Science, Product, and Business teams to ensure scalable, production\-grade outcomes.



Now, if you were to come on board as our AI Manager, we’d ask you to do the following:

* Oversee the design, development, and deployment of scalable AI solutions across the organization;
* Provide strategic direction for AI initiatives while ensuring alignment with business objectives;
* Manage and mentor a multidisciplinary team of AI Engineers, ML Engineers, and Data Scientists;
* Lead technical architecture decisions, system design, and solution reviews;
* Foster a culture of engineering excellence, code quality, and continuous improvement;
* Collaborate with Product and Engineering leaders to scope features and prioritize development efforts;
* Stay informed on cutting\-edge AI advancements (e.g., LLMs, RAG, vector databases) and evaluate their practical application within the company;
* Establish best practices and frameworks for model development, MLOps, and scalable deployment;
* Present complex AI concepts and project outcomes to technical and non\-technical stakeholders.



Think you have what it takes to be our AI Manager? Here’s how we’ll know:

* 5\+ years of hands\-on experience delivering AI / data products, including at least 2 years in a leadership role;
* Deep technical expertise in areas such as Large Language Models (LLMs), Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG), embeddings, and vector search;
* Strong software engineering fundamentals, including experience with Python and data science tools (NumPy, pandas, etc.);
* Proven track record of deploying AI models into production in cloud\-based environments (AWS, GCP, or Azure);
* Experience managing teams and projects in agile environments with strong prioritization skills;
* Familiarity with modern data platforms, database systems (SQL \& NoSQL), and RESTful APIs;
* Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to explain AI concepts to non\-technical audiences;
* A growth mindset, with a passion for mentoring, coaching, and developing high\-performing teams.

Compass Group Canada is committed to nurturing a diverse workforce representative of the communities within which we operate. We encourage and are pleased to consider all qualified candidates, without regard to race, colour, citizenship, religion, sex, marital / family status, sexual orientation, gender identity, aboriginal status, age, disability or persons who may require an accommodation, to apply.



For accommodation requests during the hiring process, please contact PeopleHub@compass\-canada.com for further information.

We are CDAI—the data and artificial intelligence engine of Compass Group North America. We design and deliver custom, in\-house solutions tailored to the unique complexities of food service and hospitality. Our work is grounded in strong data foundations, layered with AI to enhance forecasting, streamline operations, and enable better, faster decision\-making across Compass Group. With deep integration into the business and a commitment to white\-glove service, CDAI empowers associates, clients, and customers through innovative, future\-forward technologies.

**Job Summary**
---------------


Job Summary We are looking for a skilled and motivated AI Engineer to join our forward\-thinking team. The ideal candidate is passionate about building cutting\-edge AI solutions, has a strong technical foundation, and excels in collaborative environments. As an AI Engineer, you will play a key role in designing, developing, and maintaining advanced data products and AI\-powered applications. You’ll work closely with cross\-functional teams—including Data Scientists, Analytics Engineers, Front\-End Developers, and ML Engineers—to deliver scalable and impactful solutions.



Now, if you were to come on board as our AI Engineer, we’d ask you to do the following:

* Develop and maintain scalable AI applications from concept to deployment;
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features;
* Architect and implement efficient and reusable AI systems;
* Write clean, well\-documented, and maintainable code following best practices;
* Conduct code reviews, provide constructive feedback and mentor junior team members;
* Staying up\-to\-date with emerging AI technologies and industry trends to drive continuous improvement.



Think you have what it takes to be our AI Engineer? Here’s how we’ll know:

* Bachelor's degree in a STEM field (or equivalent experience);
* Strong experience with Large Language Models (LLMs), RAG, embeddings;
* 2\+ years of experience developing AI / data products in a hands\-on capacity;
* Proficiency in the modern data science stack (Python, NumPy, pandas);
* Strong cloud engineering skills and ample experience taking AI ideas to production;
* Experience with database systems (SQL and NoSQL) and data warehouses;
* Familiarity with RESTful APIs;
* Knowledge of version control systems (e.g., Git) and agile development methodologies;
* Excellent problem\-solving skills, attention to detail, and ability to work independently or in a team environment;
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills with experience in relaying complex concepts to non\-technical users.

Compass Group Canada is committed to nurturing a diverse workforce representative of the communities within which we operate. We encourage and are pleased to consider all qualified candidates, without regard to race, colour, citizenship, religion, sex, marital / family status, sexual orientation, gender identity, aboriginal status, age, disability or persons who may require an accommodation, to apply.



For accommodation requests during the hiring process, please contact PeopleHub@compass\-canada.com for further information.

We are recruiting a **Data Scientist IA** to reinforce our team in Valladolid with on\-site work.


**What we are looking for:**


* Master's in Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, or another quantitative field;
* 3 years of experience (minimum) with Data Science;
* Strong problem\-solving skills with a focus on end\-to\-end IA solutions in a production environment;
* Proficient in using statistical computer languages (Python, SQL, etc.) to manipulate data and derive insights from large datasets;
* Hands\-on experience with MLOps methodologies and technologies for AI use cases, covering deployment, monitoring, and maintenance;
* Experience in deploying, monitoring, and securing Machine Learning models in Google Cloud Platform;
* Experience with containerization technologies like Docker and container orchestration tools such as Kubernetes;
* Experience with API REST or MQTT;
* Strong understanding of CI/CD pipelines and version control systems;
* A proactive drive to learn and master new technologies and methodologies, particularly in the realm of MLOps;
* Fluent in English.


**What we have to offer:**


* Flexibility in the work regime (on\-site);
* Opportunity for professional growth in a growing company;
* Collaborative and supportive work environment;
* Competitive benefits package.


If you identify with this profile, send us your updated CV to recrutamento@movilges.com



If you want to learn more about us:



Movilges IT Consulting has over 30 years of experience in the Spanish market, specializing in Logistics, Mobility, and IT. We offer consulting services, application development, and system maintenance. Just as the technological universe is constantly evolving, Movilges IT Consulting aims to evolve as well, increasing its presence in Portugal. We strive not only to provide the best services to partners and clients but also to offer the best conditions, benefits, and professional growth opportunities for our entire team.



In Portugal, we are present in different sectors such as technology, health, public administration, energy, services, banking, and insurance.



By submitting your application, you authorize Movilges IT Consulting to process your personal data, such as name, email, phone number, and information about your academic and professional experiences as stated in your CV. The processing of this data serves only the legitimate purposes of the company, i.e., for the recruitment processes of qualified professionals for our team. For any questions related to your personal data, you can contact us at portugal@movilges.com
